--TEST--
`as Shape` from an operand that can hold no object is `E0708`, and a shape with a `secret` field has nothing a run-time test can check and stays `E0711` — `rule:types/conversion`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A shape is tested by walking the object's fields, so an operand that is
// never an object shares no value with it: the refusal a class target gets.
type Pad = {top: float, left: float};
int $n = 3;
$n as Pad;
string $s = "x";
$s as {a: int};
// A qualifier is erased before the program runs, so the walk could not check
// this field. `is` refuses the same shape with `E0813`.
type Hidden = {key: secret string};
mixed $m = 3;
$m as Hidden;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0708]: `int` cannot be converted to `{left: float, top: float}`
  --> %s:6:1
  |
6 | $n as Pad;
  | ^^^^^^^^^ converted here
  = help: `rule:types/conversion` converts into a shape by testing the value's fields, and no value of this type is an object that could have them

error[E0708]: `string` cannot be converted to `{a: int}`
  --> %s:8:1
  |
8 | $s as {a: int};
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ converted here
  = help: `rule:types/conversion` converts into a shape by testing the value's fields, and no value of this type is an object that could have them

error[E0711]: `mixed` cannot be converted to `{key: secret string}`
   --> %s:13:1
   |
13 | $m as Hidden;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^ converted here
   = help: There is no checked conversion into this type, because it cannot be tested at run time. Convert to a declared class, a `Core` class such as `Core\Time\Date`, or a shape such as `{id: int}`. A shape cannot have a `secret` field here.

error: aborting due to 3 errors
